.TH SHMAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
shmat \- attach a System V shared memory segment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/shm.h>
.B void* shmat(int id, const void* address, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Attaches a segment, using a kernel\-chosen address when address is NULL.
Flags include SHM_RDONLY, SHM_RND, SHM_REMAP and SHM_EXEC.
Detach the returned address with shmdt.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the attachment address, or the \-1 pointer sentinel with errno set.
Use map_failed to check the sentinel without dereferencing it.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shmdt (3crunch),
.BR shmget (3crunch),
.BR shmat (2)
